---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import {site} from '../config';
---
<Base title="Contact GuideHollow Sheets" description="Send a private question or report a spreadsheet guide correction, broken link, or tool problem to the GuideHollow Sheets operator." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Contact',url:'/contact/'}]}><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Help make the working clearer</p><h1>A correction is<br/>a useful next step.</h1><p>Found a mismatched result or an instruction that no longer fits your app? Let us know.</p></header><article class="prose info-content"><h2>Private correspondence</h2><p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. This is the operator's established GuideHollow contact address, also used for GuideHollow Sheets. Do not send a real workbook, personal records, passwords or API keys unless an appropriate, separate sharing arrangement has been agreed.</p><h2>Public issues and source history</h2><p>You can <a href={`${site.repository}/issues/new`}>open an issue in the GuideHollow Sheets repository</a>. A GitHub account is required to submit an issue, and its content is public. <a href={`${site.repository}/issues`}>Read existing issues</a> before reporting a duplicate.</p><h2>A useful report includes</h2><ul><li>The page URL and affected formula or instruction.</li><li>Your app, version and locale when relevant.</li><li>A small fictional input that reproduces the problem, with expected and observed results.</li><li>The exact error, without personal data or credentials.</li><li>An official documentation link if it helps establish the correction.</li></ul><p>We cannot guarantee a response time or provide individualized financial, legal or professional advice. A report starts an editorial review; it is not an agreement to access a private account or change a workbook.</p><h2>Privacy questions</h2><p>Use email for a question that should not be public. Share only what is needed to explain it. Our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy notice</a> describes the site's local tools, hosting and correspondence.</p></article></Base>
